Total outcomes of a dice = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}
[Standard dice outcomes]
Odd numbers = {1, 3, 5}
Numbers divisible by 5 = {5}
Union set (Odd or divisible by 5) = {1, 3, 5}
[Combine sets, remove duplicate 5]
Number of favourable outcomes = 3
[Count of outcomes]
Probability = \( \frac{3}{6} = \frac{1}{2} \)
[Favourable outcomes divided by total outcomes]
Result: \( \frac{1}{2} \) [Ans.]
